# M13 Phase 3 (#109): other-platform native libs gathered here before a multi-RID `pixi run pack`
/artifacts/

# Claude Code local subagent worktrees (isolation: worktree). Narrowly scoped so shared config
# under .claude/ (agents/, commands/, settings.json) stays committable without `git add -f`.
.claude/worktrees/


# Vendor documentation survey output (#527): a mirrored copy of both vendors public docs plus
# the derived index. Regenerate with `pixi run vendor-survey`; never commit ~7MB of vendor text.
.vendor-survey/

# ...except the derived index itself, which is 19KB rather than 7MB and is the one file
# `audit-completeness` reads (#589). Its own header states its purpose -- "EVERY page with a
# disposition, so coverage is checkable not asserted" -- and that is exactly what CI does with it;
# without it committed, the audit cannot run anywhere but a machine that has already run the survey.
#
# It is a SNAPSHOT: re-running `pixi run vendor-survey` regenerates it, and the regenerated file must
# be committed with that change or CI validates a stale index while the real corpus has moved.
# Nothing flags that today -- tracked in #620 alongside the rest of the check-that-a-check-runs work.
!.vendor-survey/ledger.tsv

# tools/aer-agy-loop/dispatch.py's generated workflow/bindings/task-dir per run -- transient
# per-invocation scaffolding, never the deliverable.
/aer-agy-loop-scratch/

# `aer dispatch` per-run room dirs (artifacts, redirected .gemini_home, flow log) -- transient
# per-invocation working state, never the deliverable.
/.aer/

# Python bytecode. Four .pyc files were tracked, so every tool run dirtied the tree.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Session-local gates captures — never evidence, never committed (a stale one shipped as a false gates record once)
gates-run.txt
gates-output.txt
gates-exit.txt
